Quick care summary to help it thrive:
- Light: bright, indirect light (avoid hot direct sun). Tolerates lower light but grows slower.  
- Water: water when the top ~1 inch (2–3 cm) of soil is dry; avoid waterlogging.  
- Soil & pot: well-draining potting mix and a pot with drainage holes.  
- Temperature & humidity: 65–75°F (18–24°C) ideal; tolerates typical home humidity—occasional misting helps.  
- Fertilizer: balanced houseplant fertilizer monthly in spring/summer; cut back in fall/winter.  
- Repot/maintenance: repot every 1–2 years or when rootbound; trim brown tips and remove dead leaves.  
- Propagation: easy from plantlets (“spiderettes”)—root them in water or soil.  
- Pets: generally considered non-toxic to cats and dogs, though pets may chew leaves and sometimes vomit.

